            "text": "{\"output\":\"=== README.md ===\\n# Service component\\n\\nFix stream_rows(resource, transform) in src/service.py so each started iterator closes its resource exactly once on exhaustion, explicit generator.close(), iteration errors and transformation errors. A transform failure propagates and no further row is read. Keep processing lazy, preserving order and transformed values; constructing or closing an unstarted generator performs no read or close. If cleanup also raises while an iteration or transform error is active, preserve the original error; otherwise propagate the cleanup error. src/consumer.py.take must close the iterator after taking its requested positive number of rows or if consuming fails. A limit of zero returns [] without starting the stream. Start in src/service.py and src/consumer.py. Resource.read_next() returns None at EOF.\\n\\nRun `python3 checks/public.py` from the project root. Implementation belongs in src/. Add checks under checks/.\\n\\n=== src/service.py ===\\ndef stream_rows(resource, transform):$\\n    while True:$\\n        row = resource.read_next()$\\n        if row is None:$\\n            break$\\n...\\ndef stream_rows(resource, transform):\\n    while True:\\n        row = resource.read_next()\\n        if row is None:\\n            break\\n        yield transform(row)\\n    resource.close()\\n\\n=== src/consumer.py ===\\nfrom .service import stream_rows\\n\\ndef take(resource, transform, limit):\\n    stream = stream_rows(resource, transform)\\n    result = []\\n    for row in stream:\\n        result.append(row)\\n        if len(result) >= limit:\\n            break\\n    return result\\n\\n=== src/resource.py ===\\nclass Rows:\\n    def __init__(self, rows):\\n        self.rows = list(rows)\\n        self.index = 0\\n        self.reads = 0\\n        self.closes = 0\\n\\n    def read_next(self):\\n        self.reads += 1\\n        if self.index == len(self.rows):\\n            return None\\n        value = self.rows[self.index]\\n        self.index += 1\\n        return value\\n\\n    def close(self):\\n        self.closes += 1\\n\\n=== src/__init__.py ===\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"signal\":null,\"cancelled\":false,\"timeout\":false,\"truncated\":false}"
